---
import { Logo } from '@ds';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/sections/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy · The Honest Agent"
  description="What thehonestagent.dev collects when you visit it, why, and your rights under the GDPR."
>
  <div class="s-privacy">
    <nav class="nav">
      <a class="home" href="/" aria-label="The Honest Agent"><Logo markSrc="/assets/robot.png" size={40} /></a>
      <div class="links">
        <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
        <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/jlcoto/the_honest_agent">GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </nav>
    <main class="body">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="sub">What this website collects when you visit it, why, and your rights under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).</p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 20 November 2026</p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>The controller for this website is:</p>
      <p class="addr">José Luis Coto Zevallos<br />The Groundlayer<br />Neumannstr. 127<br />13189 Berlin, Germany<br /><a href="mailto:jose@thegroundlayer.io">jose@thegroundlayer.io</a></p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>This website, its documentation and the video on the home page are hosted by Cloudflare, Inc. (101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). To deliver the pages and protect them from attacks, Cloudflare processes technical data such as your IP address, the date and time of the request, and information about your browser.</p>
      <p>Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, our legitimate interest in running the website securely and reliably. Cloudflare is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.</p>

      <h2>Web analytics</h2>
      <p>We use PostHog to understand how people use this website: which pages they read, where they come from, and which links and buttons they click. This helps us see which parts of the documentation are useful and which need work.</p>
      <p>PostHog runs in cookieless mode. It sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser's local or session storage. For each page view and click, it records:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the page address and the page you came from</li>
        <li>your browser, operating system, device type and screen size</li>
        <li>the element you clicked, such as a link or a button</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Your IP address is removed before the event is processed and is not stored. PostHog counts visitors with an anonymous identifier that it calculates on its servers, so we can tell how many people visited without knowing who they are. We don't record sessions, build profiles, or combine this data with any other source.</p>
      <p>The data is stored in PostHog Cloud EU, in Frankfurt, Germany. PostHog processes it on our behalf under a data processing agreement (Art. 28 GDPR). Requests reach PostHog through our own address, m.thehonestagent.dev, which PostHog runs on Cloudflare's network. PostHog keeps the data for about one year and then deletes it.</p>
      <p>Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, our legitimate interest in understanding how the website is used so we can improve it. You can object at any time (see your rights below), or block the requests with a content blocker in your browser.</p>

      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>This website links to GitHub, X, LinkedIn, Substack and the documentation of other products. Nothing from those sites is loaded until you click a link. Once you do, their own privacy policies apply.</p>

      <h2>Contact by email</h2>
      <p>If you email us, we process your message and address to answer you. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR if your message is about a contract, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. Emails are handled through Google Workspace (Google Ireland Limited).</p>

      <h2>The honest-agent tool</h2>
      <p>The honest-agent command-line tool and the reports it generates run on your own machine. They send nothing to this website or to us.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to access your data (Art. 15 GDPR), to have it corrected (Art. 16), deleted (Art. 17) or its processing restricted (Art. 18), to data portability (Art. 20), and to object to processing based on our legitimate interest (Art. 21). To use any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:jose@thegroundlayer.io">jose@thegroundlayer.io</a>.</p>
      <p>You also have the right to complain to a data protection supervisory authority, for example the Berlin Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information (Berliner Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit).</p>
    </main>
  </div>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
.s-privacy{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#FFFFFF 0,#EEF0E8 480px);color:var(--fg-1);font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:15px;line-height:1.6}
.nav{max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto;padding:20px 32px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px 24px}
.home{display:inline-flex;text-decoration:none;color:var(--fg-1)}
.links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:8px 24px}
.links a{color:var(--fg-2);text-decoration:none;font-weight:500}
.links a:hover{color:var(--fg-1)}
.body{max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;padding:32px 32px 72px}
h1{margin:0 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:500;font-size:44px;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.02em}
.sub{margin:0 0 28px;font-size:18px;color:var(--fg-2)}
h2{margin:32px 0 8px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:500;font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.body p,.body li{color:var(--fg-2)}
.body p{margin:0 0 14px}
.body ul{margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px}
.body li{margin:0 0 4px}
.body a{color:var(--green-700);font-weight:500;text-decoration:none;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
.body a:hover{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
.updated{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px;color:var(--fg-3)!important}
@media (max-width:900px){
 .nav{padding:16px}
 .body{padding:20px 16px 56px}
 h1{font-size:34px}
 .sub{font-size:16px;margin-bottom:20px}
 h2{font-size:21px}
}
</style>
